    "ASGinzburg/FiniteDimensionalRegularExtComparison.lean": "Final source6e446474... has two existing theorem-scoped transparency options and two extra ←Category.assoc rewrites in diagonal/off-diagonal action cases. These merely reparenthesize the exact original three composable morphisms so the same generated inclusion_assoc theorem applies. Same regular coproduct action, original Ext postcomposition, canonical coproduct/direct-sum/total-algebra equivalences and actual left action preserved. Original8 headers and all data definitions unchanged, [simp]/[reassoc] attributes preserved. Moving scoped option before existing doc comment ensures same declaration-local scope.",
    "ASGinzburg/FiniteProjectivePresentations.lean": "Right/left existing Epi proofs each get one scoped option and proof-local alias f equal to underlying LinearMap of the exact original evaluated finiteFreeModuleπ. Pinned ModuleCat Hom.hom projects that same map. Both change steps retain same y basis preimage, same original H:f(y j)=b j, same coefficient sum ∑j b.repr x j • y j and original basis.sum_repr. No new map, scalar action, arbitrary preimage, chosen basis, support, public assumption or definition changes. All original22 headers/context retained.",
    "ASGinzburg/GinzburgASProjectiveResolution.lean": "Only scoped option and removal of one dsimp step in original QuasiIso proof. Same augmentation toSingle0Equiv uses simpleRightModuleπ and D1-zero condition; exactness/epi transfer, original identity ShortComplex iso, degree0 ChainComplex.of_d and higher exactness proof preserved. Original ProjectiveResolution complex, projective,π,quasiIso fields and genuine GinzburgRegular hypothesis unchanged; all4 headers exact checkpoint9.",
    "ASGinzburg/GinzburgArrowOppositeClasses.lean": "Original ordinary one-arrow path-opposite equality adds reflexivity after same Path.toList_injective/simp. No path formula change: same Path.snoc nil arrow, reversed list and arrow endpoints. Two original reflection/Jacobian-entry theorems get scoped transparency options only; same opposite potential, reflected sheet1-s, original height transports and genuine first/third Jacobian classes retained. All7 headers exact checkpoint9.",
    "ASGinzburg/GinzburgFirstADualFormula.lean": "One theorem-scoped option only. Original canonical A-dual first differential, actual representable Hom coordinates, same original-arrow column, incoming-generator indexing and complete original Yoneda/precomposition proof preserved. Entire checkpoint9 source byte-exact after deleting the added option.",
